1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,570
Last time, the shape.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:07,720
This time, how a carpenter
marks it out and cuts it, so

3
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:11,850
the upper piece drops in
and tightens as it seats.

4
00:00:12,333 --> 00:00:16,883
We'll follow one training
course's sequence, step by step.

5
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:19,503
Others may order things differently.

6
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:28,297
First, decide which piece is which.

7
00:00:28,907 --> 00:00:32,487
The male is the upper
piece, and it's the one

8
00:00:32,527 --> 00:00:35,297
that takes the anchor
bolt, beside the joint.

9
00:00:36,227 --> 00:00:39,957
Mark each piece clearly
before you lay anything out.

10
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,270
Then the center lines, as in Episode 1.

11
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:48,380
The dovetail is laid out
from them, evenly on either

12
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,750
side, so they need to be
right before anything else.

13
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:59,883
On the female piece, start on
the top face with the end line.

14
00:01:00,373 --> 00:01:01,943
Then the seat lines.

15
00:01:02,773 --> 00:01:08,823
Then the dovetail lines, laid out evenly
on either side of the center line.

16
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:13,853
The sides of the dovetail are
angled using the width of the

17
00:01:13,893 --> 00:01:19,043
sashigane's blade, running from the
seat line toward the dovetail line.

18
00:01:20,133 --> 00:01:23,823
Finally, the seat lines are
carried down both side faces.

19
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:29,757
On the male piece:

20
00:01:30,167 --> 00:01:34,897
the end line, the tip of the
dovetail, and the cut lines.

21
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,857
Now cut the female.

22
00:01:40,587 --> 00:01:45,277
Rip in from the end along
the seat line, splitting it.

23
00:01:46,447 --> 00:01:50,067
Then crosscut down to
it, also splitting the

24
00:01:50,107 --> 00:01:54,057
line, and the waste above
the seat comes away.

25
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:59,413
Rip the sides of the dovetail
socket, splitting the line, without

26
00:01:59,453 --> 00:02:04,043
sawing past the end of the
dovetail or into the seat below.

27
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:08,260
Chop out the socket, keeping the chisel's

28
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:12,430
flat back toward the
outside of the socket.

29
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,690
Then work down to the level of the seat.

30
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,110
One detail matters:

31
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:25,910
at the tip, dig the socket about three
millimeters deeper than the line.

32
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:31,570
Then the tip can't touch first and
leave a gap somewhere else in the joint.

33
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:36,617
Now the male.

34
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:42,807
First cut the end square at the
end line, then carry the center

35
00:02:42,847 --> 00:02:46,517
line and the dovetail lines
onto the fresh end grain.

36
00:02:47,487 --> 00:02:52,297
Rip in to the shoulder, then
crosscut away the lower half,

37
00:02:52,507 --> 00:02:56,137
leaving the cut-back underside
that will sit on the seat.

38
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:00,610
Rip the cheeks of the
dovetail with a slight taper:

39
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:05,310
leave the line at the top,
and take it at the bottom.

40
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:10,120
The dovetail is a hair
narrower below, so it

41
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:13,710
enters easily and
tightens as it goes down.

42
00:03:14,198 --> 00:03:17,143
Crosscut the shoulders,
splitting the line.

43
00:03:17,913 --> 00:03:21,173
Then chisel away what the
saw couldn't reach in the

44
00:03:21,213 --> 00:03:24,823
corners, and chamfer the
edges with the chisel.

45
00:03:28,433 --> 00:03:32,563
Test the fit by dropping
the male in from above.

46
00:03:33,433 --> 00:03:39,403
If it's a little too tight, a general
carpentry manual suggests kigoroshi.

47
00:03:40,093 --> 00:03:44,603
The gennō's slightly domed
face carries the same name:

48
00:03:44,913 --> 00:03:46,483
the kigoroshi face.

49
00:03:46,967 --> 00:03:49,997
And remember why the tip was dug deep:

50
00:03:50,607 --> 00:03:55,017
the joint should bear everywhere
else, never on its tip.

51
00:03:58,633 --> 00:04:00,583
Next time, a new joint:

52
00:04:01,013 --> 00:04:04,554
the mortise and tenon, hozo and hozo-ana.

53
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:07,310
Center lines first.

54
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:10,230
Mark the female, then the male.

55
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:17,310
Cut to the lines you chose, taper the
cheeks, and let it drop in and tighten.

56
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,330
One note:

57
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:33,620
sharp-tool technique, and how
to use these tools safely, is

58
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:37,790
best learned from a teacher,
at a bench, in person.
